Fix v0.BitriseYMLConfigUpdateParams.location generation

The upstream Bitrise swagger spec models the `location` property as:

    "allOf": [ { "$ref": "#/definitions/website.BitriseYMLLocation" } ]

with a sibling `description` and `example`. That is a standard
Swagger 2.0 idiom (JSON Schema draft-4 ignores sibling keywords next
to a bare `$ref`, so `allOf` is the documented workaround). But
go-swagger unconditionally routes single-ref `allOf` through its
composed-object path and emits:

    Location struct { WebsiteBitriseYMLLocation } `json:"location,omitempty"`

which JSON-marshals to `{"location":{"WebsiteBitriseYMLLocation":"repository"}}`
instead of the plain string the Bitrise API expects. This is a
long-standing generator bug (go-swagger #436, #740; PR #1849 added
partial type-alias support at definition level but not for scalar
refs used inline in a property).

Drop the `allOf` wrapper and use a bare `$ref` on the property so
go-swagger emits the type-aliased form:

    Location WebsiteBitriseYMLLocation `json:"location,omitempty"`

The tradeoff is that the property-level `description` is dropped from
the spec; the description on the referenced enum type is preserved.

Remove this patch once go-swagger collapses single-scalar-ref `allOf`
to an alias on its own, or once the upstream Bitrise spec stops
wrapping the enum in `allOf`.

--- a/swagger.json
+++ b/swagger.json
@@ -9918,12 +9918,7 @@
       "properties": {
         "location": {
           "description": "Location of bitrise.yml file. Enums(bitrise.io, repository)",
-          "allOf": [
-            {
-              "$ref": "#/definitions/website.BitriseYMLLocation"
-            }
-          ],
-          "example": "repository"
+          "$ref": "#/definitions/website.BitriseYMLLocation"
         }
       }
     },
